00:07:32.868 --> 00:07:36.171
HE'S HAD A LONG PERIOD MARK WITH

00:07:34.269 --> 00:07:38.574
THE PUBLIC WAS ALLOWED TO LOOK

00:07:36.305 --> 00:07:39.408
AT HIM, ASK QUESTIONS TO THE

00:07:38.707 --> 00:07:41.009
JUDICIARY COMMITTEE.

00:07:39.541 --> 00:07:41.777
IF SENATORS HAVE ASKED HIM

00:07:41.143 --> 00:07:43.779
QUESTIONS IN PUBLIC AND PRIVATE.

00:07:41.910 --> 00:07:46.615
ALL THAT HAS TAKEN PLACE AND ALL

00:07:43.912 --> 00:07:48.283
THAT WAS THERE FOR A REASON.

00:07:46.748 --> 00:07:49.084
PEOPLE ARE THERE TO DECIDE WHAT

00:07:48.417 --> 00:07:51.587
THEY THINK AND WHETHER THE

00:07:49.217 --> 00:07:52.287
SENATORS WILL VOTE FOR HIM OR

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:52.621
NOT AND THEY'RE ALLOWED TO DO

00:07:52.421 --> 00:07:54.490
THAT.

00:07:52.754 --> 00:07:56.625
BUT IT CAN'T BE THAT WHEN PEOPLE

00:07:54.623 --> 00:07:59.027
MAKE LAST-MINUTE ALLEGATIONS AND

00:07:56.758 --> 00:08:01.363
THROW CHARACTER ASSASSINATION AT

00:07:59.194 --> 00:08:05.400
HIM THAT THERE FOR THE ANSWER TO

00:08:01.497 --> 00:08:06.068
STEP BACK AND DO NOT GO FORWARD.

00:08:05.534 --> 00:08:06.768
THESE PEOPLE DESERVE TO HAVE

00:08:06.201 --> 00:08:09.037
THEIR HEARING IN THE SENATORS

00:08:06.902 --> 00:08:09.538
DESERVE TO VOTE AS THEY THINK

00:08:09.171 --> 00:08:11.073
THEY SHOULD.

00:08:09.671 --> 00:08:12.241
&gt;&gt; Bret: AND HE'S IN IT FOR

00:08:11.206 --> 00:08:12.608
THE LONG HAUL.

00:08:12.374 --> 00:08:14.476
&gt;&gt; YES.

